From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lagz0ne <15101444+lagz0ne@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 02:16:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 11/20] feat(embed): sign host apps' reviewers in to one canvas
 through a short-lived token

doop stays one backend for several host apps, but nobody logs in
to it: each host shows doop's review panel in an iframe and signs its user in
itself. This is the server side of that.

- POST /api/auth/embed/session (server/embed.ts, a better-auth plugin
  endpoint so it can set the session cookie) takes the host's HS256 token:
  iss (a host in DOOP_EMBED_HOSTS), aud "doop", sub, name, canvas, role
  (view | comment | review, never edit), iat/exp at most five minutes apart,
  a jti used once (in-memory first-use check plus a verification row across
  restarts). Every failure is one 401; the reason goes to the log. It is
  behind formCsrfMiddleware, as sign-in is: a browser's request needs a
  trusted Origin even before it holds a cookie (no login CSRF).
- It finds or creates a shadow user, <hash(iss, sub)>@<iss>.embed.invalid,
  with no password or OAuth account and no first canvas (auth.ts letIn: the
  after-create hook runs after the endpoint's scope, so it is told by the
  endpoint's path), and starts an ordinary session for two hours. The grant
  lives on the SESSION (session.embed_canvas_id / embed_role, migration 0049
  generated with drizzle-kit), not the user, so the shadow user holds no
  access anywhere and the grant ends with the session.
- An embed session opens its one canvas at its one role (callerRole,
  connRole, the WS join), reaches only EMBED_ROUTES (the /api session gate
  answers 403 for the rest: dashboard, new canvases, agent keys, frame
  edits, memory...), and reads the canvas and its room through the reviewer
  filter: frames, pages, comments with replies and resolves, approvals,
  presence without status; not tasks, feedback, activity, decisions,
  proposals, references or guidelines (forReviewer, canvasForReviewer).
- Contract for the panel: DOOP_EMBED_HOSTS = {"<id>": {"secret": "<32+>",
  "origin": "https://<host page>"}}; the answer is { canvasId, role,
  hostOrigin, expiresAt, user: { name } }; embedHostOrigins() lists the host
  pages for the panel's frame-ancestors (empty = no panel).
- The panel may be served from its own hostname, so its host-only cookie
  never replaces a person's own doop session: nothing reads the request
  host, and that origin goes in TRUSTED_ORIGINS.
- Operator and admin user lists hide shadow reviewers unless ?all=1.

tests/embed.test.ts (real servers): the answer and a host-only cookie;
confinement (another canvas, the dashboard, new canvases, agent keys, frame
and memory edits refused; versions, comments and a verdict allowed); the
reviewer filter over REST, the room's init and live messages; replayed,
expired, forged, over-long, edit-role and bad-canvas tokens refused; the
shadow user cannot sign in, owns nothing and is hidden from lists; host
origins parsed; and a production-mode server on a second hostname refusing
an untrusted panel origin and working once it is in TRUSTED_ORIGINS
(vitest's TEST=true turns better-auth's origin check off, so that case
clears it). With 0010: 61 related test files, 486 tests pass.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
